# Production build settings. COMMITTED — this file holds no secrets.
#
# ── Why this file has to exist ──
# Vite loads `.env.local` in EVERY mode, including `build`. Local development sets
# VITE_USE_EMULATORS=true there, so without this file `npm run build` produces a
# deployable bundle that tries to reach 127.0.0.1:9099 for auth, :8080 for Firestore
# and :5001 for functions.
#
# That failure is nasty precisely because it is not a build error: the bundle deploys
# cleanly, Hosting serves it, and every user sees an app that hangs on sign-in with
# nothing in the console but connection refused to an address that only exists on one
# developer's laptop.
#
# `.env.[mode]` outranks `.env.local` in Vite's precedence order, so this wins for
# production builds no matter what a developer has set locally — which is the point.
VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false
